WEBVTT

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.250
Major General Dylan.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:28.290
Major Loki.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.380
I hear that the Mistilteinn is complete.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:37.430
It was a great sacrifice.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:41.070
The number of lives that were lost

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:43.890
in order to retrieve data 
on how to defeat it...

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.350
But now,

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.970
we can mark their names in history.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.510
This Mistilteinn

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.190
will defeat the Basilisk.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:31.070
<b><i>Unlimited Fafnir</i></b>

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:45.390
<b>Front Line in Distant Waters</b>

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:52.520
There's so much smoke.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:55.010
It's higher than I thought.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:06.630
Tear?

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:17.000
So we're finally fighting the Basilisk,

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:18.850
aren't we?

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:29.480
Don't be so nervous.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.850
We're still quite far from the Basilisk.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.810
The battle will probably begin in three days.

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:37.570
Three days...

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:39.580
Tachikawa Honoka.

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:40.410
Yes?

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:42.580
<i>Honoka?</i>

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:51.120
It's so cute.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:53.290
Did you make these, Honoka?

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:58.170
Yes, I received data about this 
volcanic island from Shinomiya-sensei.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:01.890
Elevation: 1,560 meters.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:05.140
Still a very active volcano, I see.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:08.120
I want to go to this caramel lake.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.350
Caldera lake.

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:11.440
There are hot springs, too.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:13.920
I've never been to a hot spring before.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.710
Okay, let's all go, then.

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:19.360
The eggs they make at hot springs are delicious.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:20.820
Okay.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.360
Hot spring eggs...

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:27.660
I see... Hot springs, huh?

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:30.620
You're all back to your usual selves.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:33.700
Right now, I want you to get plenty of rest

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:35.520
and prepare for the battle.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:36.650
Right!

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:41.780
Honoka.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:42.470
Hm?

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:44.070
Thanks.

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:45.180
It's nothing.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.850
I like making that sort of thing.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:50.600
You know, Tear...

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:55.640
She has a lot of painful memories.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.520
Yet she's smiling happily.

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:00.540
Thanks.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:02.480
It's nothing.

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:05.450
All right, let's go!

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:12.920
I want to go to the hot springs, but...

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:14.040
Mononobe-kun.

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:19.710
What did you need?

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.840
I wanted to thank you.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:23.380
Thank me?

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.410
About Lisa and Mitsuki.

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:29.940
You said something to them, right?

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:34.140
Oh, yeah, but nothing's resolved yet.

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:37.530
But they're moving forward now.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:38.880
So...

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:41.040
To thank you.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:45.330
A one-day hot spring ticket?

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:47.840
Effective today only?

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:49.840
Yeah.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.990
You want to go, don't you, Mononobe-kun?

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:54.740
Sure I do.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:57.760
But I'm the only guy.

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:00.620
It might cause trouble if I ran into anyone.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:03.000
That's why it's a one-day ticket.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:06.010
Is the whole place reserved for me?

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:07.000
Yeah.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:10.980
The hot spring is all yours today.

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:12.430
Have fun.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:16.180
Thanks.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:27.670
I really have to thank Fyril.

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:31.780
I'm first!

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.920
Come on, everyone!

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:42.600
We're coming.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:48.130
Are you okay, Lisa?

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:50.120
Yes, it's almost healed.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:53.050
I'll be all better by the 
time we start the mission.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:57.120
It's said that hot springs are good 
for healing wounds, too, so...

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.890
You don't have to tell me that. I know.

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:03.200
I said I'm fine alone.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:04.360
Are you sure?

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:07.070
<i>I'm not okay!</i>

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:08.880
<i>If they catch me,</i>

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:10.400
<i>a repentance essay won't cover it!</i>

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:17.450
Listen, a slow decision will lead to death.

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:21.110
<i>I can believe you now!</i>

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:22.420
I'm second!

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:29.890
Ariela-san, that's bad manners.

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:32.250
Come on, don't be such a stiff.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:34.640
There's no one else here.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.950
<i>Yes, there is! Right here!</i>

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:39.600
It's so big here! Let's swim!

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:41.360
Third.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:47.930
I'm a grown-up,

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:50.030
so I'm going to get in properly.

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:55.780
I'm going to insist I'm still a child and jump in.

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:01.400
It's a little hot.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:04.710
It has to be, or it wouldn't set the mood.

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:09.350
E-Excuse me.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:13.220
No, no, you have to take that off.

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:17.100
B-But...

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:19.880
I didn't want to at first, either,

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:21.560
but it's fun once you get used to it.

00:08:22.070 --> 00:08:24.630
What do they call it? 
A completely open relationship?

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:25.520
Yes.

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:28.060
W-Well, then...

00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:35.030
See? It's fine.

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:36.660
Yes.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.810
Actually, my glasses are so foggy

00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:41.840
that I can't really see anything,

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:44.370
so I don't feel too embarrassed.

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:47.420
I wanted Yuu to come, too.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:52.580
If Mononobe-kun were here, 
we'd all be together, huh?

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:54.940
<i>We </i>are<i> all here!</i>

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:57.750
<i>And damn it, Fyril!</i>

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:02.770
Wow, you have big breasts, Lisa-chan!

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.540
They're floating in the water.

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:07.680
S-Stop touching them!

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:10.510
They're kind of different from mine.

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:14.490
They're more soft and 
marshmallowy than bouncy.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:16.950
If you don't stop that...

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:18.700
I'll retaliate!

00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:19.930
Take this!

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:27.120
What is it, Tear-chan?

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:31.870
I'll let this go for today.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:35.340
But I'm never going to lose to you!

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:37.590
It's a competition?

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:41.110
Let's see who can hold 
her breath longer, then!

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:44.600
I won't lose!

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:49.790
Iris-san, I'm not done retaliating yet!

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:52.600
Mitsuki-chan, help!

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:57.540
Are you having fun, Mononobe-kun?

00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:00.420
Yeah, it looks like you guys are.

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:01.940
Wait, Fyril?!

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:03.410
Nice delayed reaction.

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:07.370
Wasn't it supposed to be 
reserved for me today?

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:09.080
Yeah.

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:12.260
It's the time I prepared for you.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:15.240
Do Iris and the others know I'm here?

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:16.400
No.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:17.900
They don't know.

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:23.310
I hid your clothes in the changing 
room under mine, so don't worry.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:27.390
Now you can look at naked girls in total secrecy.

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:29.350
Are you happy?

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:32.200
Wh-Why would I be?

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:36.320
Then I need to do something to make you happy.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:39.280
What should I do?

00:10:39.770 --> 00:10:42.470
W-Wait!

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:46.670
Did you hear Mononobe's voice?

00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:47.910
Nii-san's?

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:49.370
<i>Shoot!</i>

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:56.330
Dispatch?

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:00.720
Was it...

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:05.180
Was it really that unwelcome?

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:07.680
No, well...

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:09.720
I mean, it spooked me, but...

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:13.650
If I had to say one way or the other... It was fun.

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:16.610
I'm glad.

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:18.170
Yes.

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:20.160
I see.

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:21.870
Understood.

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:25.240
Everyone,

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:29.200
the operation that NIFL has 
been planning independently

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:32.170
is being carried out tomorrow.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:35.780
NIFL's?

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:47.740
<i>Long time no see, Colonel Shinomiya.</i>

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:50.260
Yes, Major General Dylan.

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:53.010
<i>Your work defeating the Kraken and Leviathan,</i>

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:56.270
<i>and warding off the Hechatoncheir,</i>

00:12:56.270 --> 00:12:57.940
<i>was impressive indeed.</i>

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:00.170
Thank you.

00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:04.030
<i>But we want you to let us handle this one.</i>

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:07.390
<i>We have a weapon that can defeat the Basilisk.</i>

00:13:08.610 --> 00:13:10.600
<i>A weapon that can defeat the Basilisk?</i>

00:13:11.630 --> 00:13:14.850
<i>As you know, the Basilisk uses 
the red beam from its eyes</i>

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:19.430
<i>to turn its targets into rock, mist, and salt.</i>

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:22.320
<i>NIFL has conducted further research,</i>

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:26.320
<i>and has determined that the red beam 
phenomenon is, in fact, weathering.</i>

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:28.660
What's weathering?

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:33.120
You know how even steel and 
concrete will rust or break down

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:38.190
if they're exposed to rain, wind, 
or sunlight for a long time?

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:41.680
<i>Weathering is a passage of time.</i>

00:13:41.680 --> 00:13:46.010
<i>In other words, its attack blows away time.</i>

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:48.970
Blows away time?

00:13:49.590 --> 00:13:52.560
<i>Having analyzed petrified material,</i>

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:55.660
<i>we've observed the passage of 
several tens of thousands of years.</i>

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:56.730
Tens of thousands?!

00:13:57.410 --> 00:13:59.170
<i>Just one second of exposure</i>

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:01.920
<i>amounts to roughly two 
thousand years of lost time.</i>

00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:05.690
You wouldn't even have time to 
become a grandma if you got hit!

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:11.120
<i>For living organisms,</i>

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:14.030
<i>it's the most dreadful weapon imaginable.</i>

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:18.580
<i>We've decided to call this a "Catastrophe."</i>

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:20.540
Catastrophe.

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:22.800
Major General Dylan,

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:25.090
what is this weapon that 
you say can oppose it?

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:29.980
<i>Time affects everything without exception.</i>

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:35.280
<i>But there are some materials 
that are resistant to aging.</i>

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:38.480
Resistant materials?

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:42.440
<i>The strongest alloy on earth: mithril.</i>

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:44.400
Mithril...

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:48.160
We've constructed a bomb

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:52.390
with a protective shell hardened 
with mithril to critical mass.

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:56.080
With it, we can defeat the Basilisk.

00:14:56.460 --> 00:14:59.040
No, we <i>must</i> defeat the Basilisk.

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:03.020
Especially for our comrades who were lost

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:05.500
for the sake of collecting this data.

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:11.320
Ren, what's wrong?

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:15.040
Ren's afraid of adult men.

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:17.910
Oh, but she's fine with you, Mononobe-kun.

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:21.120
She even said you're like an older brother.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:28.740
<i>Your subordinates are rather 
easygoing, aren't they?</i>

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:30.850
I apologize.

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:33.700
We have so many problem children.

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:36.370
<i>Then, behold the power of the large-scale</i>

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:40.910
<i>anti-Basilisk weapon developed here at NIFL...</i>

00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:43.740
<i>The Mistilteinn!</i>

00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:58.740
The operation begins in twelve hours.

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:04.930
Tear, are you scared?

00:16:05.550 --> 00:16:06.690
Yeah.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:10.860
I started shaking when I 
heard about the Basilisk.

00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:14.380
Well, it was pretty crazy.

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:17.580
Blowing away time...

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:20.130
What if it gets you?

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:22.790
Does it turn you into bone?

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:25.420
I only hope it would leave the bones.

00:16:26.690 --> 00:16:27.750
No.

00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:32.260
I don't want you and the others to die.

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:34.380
Don't worry.

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:37.820
We don't want to die, either.

00:16:37.820 --> 00:16:39.880
We'll fight so we don't turn into bone.

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:44.140
That's why we're all thinking of strategies.

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:48.610
I wish there was something I could do.

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:53.570
You're filling your role 
perfectly just by being here.

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:55.680
But...

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:57.890
Oh, yeah.

00:16:57.890 --> 00:17:00.730
It'd help if you'd cheer for us, then.

00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:05.750
I think that alone will bring our 
chances of success up really high.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:07.350
Really?

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:08.210
Yeah.

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:10.800
Cheer for us, and we'll be motivated.

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:15.070
When we're motivated, 
we can do better than usual.

00:17:15.070 --> 00:17:16.300
That's how it works.

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:18.680
Okay.

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:22.140
I'll cheer for everyone.

00:17:52.890 --> 00:17:54.690
The operation will begin shortly.

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:57.260
It's finally time.

00:17:58.020 --> 00:18:00.510
I'm informed that you'll be 
shooting it straight down.

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:04.110
<i>The Basilisk's attack range 
is roughly 5,000 meters.</i>

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:08.560
<i>We'll be dropping it from 
an altitude of 8,000 meters.</i>

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:11.880
<i>By our calculations, that's far enough 
away to withstand the red beam.</i>

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:16.280
<i>All we need to do is to drop 
it straight onto the Basilisk.</i>

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:18.490
What are the chances that it'll evade?

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:20.440
<i>According to our observations so far,</i>

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:23.880
<i>whenever the Basilisk detects 
an object heading towards it,</i>

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:26.960
<i>it stops moving to retaliate.</i>

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:29.420
And according to our calculations,

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:32.640
it won't be fast enough to 
run from the Mistilteinn.

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:33.920
<i>Mister!</i>

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:38.750
You're the one with the 
color-changed Ryumon, aren't you?

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:42.850
Thank you for protecting me, Mister.

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:45.740
I'm cheering for you.

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:47.310
Good luck!

00:19:12.190 --> 00:19:14.400
We're arrived above the target.

00:19:24.620 --> 00:19:27.020
Drop the Mistilteinn!

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:28.220
Dropping.

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:41.030
Altitude: 6,000.

00:19:41.890 --> 00:19:45.070
Entering Catastrophe range momentarily.

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:13.770
Altitude: 2,000.

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:15.640
Mistilteinn in good condition.

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:17.350
On course for impact with target.

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:24.030
Impact in five seconds.

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:54.850
Mistilteinn signal lost.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:59.120
What happened?

00:20:59.120 --> 00:20:59.940
Mister!

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:02.900
Major General Dylan, what was that?

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:06.100
Major General Dylan! Major General Dylan!

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:08.740
Mistilteinn annihilated.

00:21:09.270 --> 00:21:11.650
A new exit wound has been confirmed.

00:21:11.650 --> 00:21:16.140
It's possible that a third eye, 
not in our prior data, has emerged.

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:16.920
What?

00:21:28.990 --> 00:21:30.550
Transport vessel, respond.

00:21:30.550 --> 00:21:33.270
This is mission command. This is mission command.

00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:33.270
Major General Dylan...

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:35.260
Respond immediately.

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:41.530
Tear-san?

00:21:49.400 --> 00:21:50.830
Her Ryumon...

00:21:51.400 --> 00:21:52.660
It's hot.

00:21:53.150 --> 00:21:55.790
It's calling me.

00:21:56.400 --> 00:21:57.290
Tear-san!

00:22:01.810 --> 00:22:02.880
Mononobe...

00:23:39.810 --> 00:24:09.670
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:40.690 --> 00:23:43.650
I haven't had hot spring eggs yet.

00:23:43.650 --> 00:23:45.520
But I guess it's not the time for that.

00:23:46.110 --> 00:23:46.830
Hm?

00:23:47.270 --> 00:23:49.070
I'm Ren Miyazawa.

00:23:49.070 --> 00:23:50.600
I can talk normally.

00:23:51.170 --> 00:23:53.320
It's our turn next.

00:23:53.840 --> 00:23:55.490
We're up against the Basilisk.

00:23:55.490 --> 00:23:57.120
We'll attack in pairs.

00:23:58.200 --> 00:24:00.370
Dark matter is the fragments of souls.

00:24:00.880 --> 00:24:03.250
I hope I can manipulate them well.

00:24:04.480 --> 00:24:09.670
Next time on <i>Unlimited Fafnir</i>: 
"Red Catastrophe."

00:24:09.670 --> 00:24:19.890
<b>Illustration: Nakajima Yuka</b>
